WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
Joining us now is Republican

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.336
Congressman Byron Donalds of Florida, who

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.405
we should note serves on the House

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.340
Oversight and Reform Committees.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.241
Good morning, Congressman.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.509
Thank you for being here.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:09.909
Obviously,

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.544
we've been talking about this indictment

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.412
for Trump today.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.646
We're going to see him in the building

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:14.180
behind me in

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.815
just a matter of hours from now.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.484
Do you think the indictment helps

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:20.653
or hurts him politically?

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.088
Well, look, it

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.124
absolutely is going to help him

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.592
in a Republican primary.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:25.825
You know,

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.627
even as we speak, Republican voters

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.229
are rallying around

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.363
President Trump simply

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.932
because what they view is an indictment

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.834
that makes no sense at all, an indictment

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.302
that is pure politics

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.304
of political persecution,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:39.906
of a political enemy,

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:42.042
something that the American people

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.576
frankly despise in our country,

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:44.477
simply not for

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:46.579
me.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.682
And what about with the general election?

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.216
You're arguing

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.851
it helps him in the Republican primary.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.318
We've seen

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.287
how the potential 2024 rivals

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:54.687
for Trump

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.756
for the GOP nomination have responded.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.792
But what about the general election?

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.260
Because CNN polling has shown

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.428
that there are voters

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.897
who approve of this indictment.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.567
Well, two things.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.669
One, I saw the report about your polling.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.570
I would say, first,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.272
that people are just responding to it

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.106
based upon,

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:13.273
you know,

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.541
how you structure the poll, whatever,

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:15.608
not going to comment

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.810
But I think that as the facts

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.478
of this thing starts to really roll out,

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.113
people are going to be against us.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.781
Look, you can be against Donald Trump.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.750
You could be before Donald Trump.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.918
Those things don't matter

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.819
what we don't do

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.454
is turn the criminal justice system

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.089
against a political opponent.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.557
I think you compare

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.492
this this this mockery

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.194
of the criminal justice system

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.762
with the fact that Joe Biden

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.164
has been an absolute terrible president,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.365
won't negotiate on debt

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.733
ceiling, has left the southern border

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.001
completely wide open.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.070
Our economy is a mess.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.338
Our adversaries across

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.940
the globe are on the move.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.775
You put all those things together.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.710
It actually helps Donald Trump

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.479
become the 47th president of the

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.279
United States.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:56.816
I understand that

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.918
Republicans many of you disagree

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.220
on the merits of this case,

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:00.954
the strength of it.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:01.921
That's even something we've heard

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.323
from some legal experts.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:03.990
But when it comes to

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.658
the underlying conduct here

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.626
and what's at the heart of this,

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.496
do you think Trump is innocent?

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.197
Well, look,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.198
innocence is something

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:12.932
that we're going to see,

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.667
of course, I believe is innocent

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:15.969
because in our system of justice,

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.871
unlike what Nancy Pelosi said,

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.873
you're innocent until proven guilty.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.841
But putting that aside,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.409
you have a prosecutor

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.211
who, by the way, is not paying attention

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.480
to the felonies that are being committed

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.015
in Manhattan today.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.050
Yesterday, last week, last month.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.851
He has decided

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.320
he wants to focus on some random

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:37.524
FEC quasi issue that even the FEC

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.691
did not go after,

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.093
that the department of Justice

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.294
did not go after.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.263
And he's using some misdemeanor

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.964
in New York state law.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.665
In my view,

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.000
Alvin Bragg is outside

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.102
of his jurisdiction as a prosecutor.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:49.802
No one

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.238
and no to every basic legal analyst,

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.673
every person who knows the law

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.941
and said he's created this theory

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.476
that's never existed.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.777
So ask yourself,

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.479
what Republican or independent

00:02:59.479 --> 00:02:59.913
or frankly,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.981
American would not think that this

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.650
is bogus and it's political

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:06.819
but do you think it's hard

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.220
to argue

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.054
that when we haven't

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.990
actually seen the indictment yet, guys,

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.226
I don't think so.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.594
I think it's very easy to argue

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.462
that when we see the indictment,

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.164
obviously, it'll be out later today.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.433
I think it'll just put

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.668
more hair

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.403
on this situation for people to see.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.404
Now, the details

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.439
about how hard he's trying to jump

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.907
through these legal hoops,

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.609
but the baseline issues

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:30.710
that have already been leaked

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.212
and been reported on.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.380
I probably doubt that, though.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.014
They'll fray

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.150
they'll they'll go much further away

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.384
than what we already know.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.019
We'll see when the indictment comes.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.955
But these initial judgments

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:42.889
about the indictment

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.257
of a former president,

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.491
when it's not crystal

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.460
clear in the minds of the American people

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.962
or the media for that matter,

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.230
what the actual elements

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.497
of the situation are.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.633
That is why you have high skepticism.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.567
And frankly,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.236
you have people who are disgusted

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.371
by what they're seeing from Alvin Bragg

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.339
and Brian from the air

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.007
and from his DA's office. Right now,

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.110
So just to be clear, is

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.311
there anything in this indictment,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:05.812
Congressman,

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:06.946
that could potentially change

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:10.483
your mind of how you were viewing this

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.518
Well, look, I got to see what he's got.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.353
But, you know,

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.520
this is going to be the layup

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.156
and this is going to be the action before

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.024
the arraignment.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.059
I'm not impressed. Not at all.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.296
Especially when Alvin Bragg, he ran on

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.697
getting Donald Trump

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:25.198
like he didn't

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.233
run on safe streets in Manhattan.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.135
He ran on getting the former president.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.870
So already his mindset,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.905
his political judgment is tainted.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:36.409
To make a move like this makes no sense.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.277
It's not very clear,

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.745
except if you're trying to,

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:39.112
you know,

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:39.912
be a star

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.281
say you're the one that got him,

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.982
so on and so forth.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.317
It's really unfortunate.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.019
I know the reporting has been about

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.453
how historic this is.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:48.588
This is an historic

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.490
this is an infamous day in America.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.127
Well, it is historic

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.361
just by the nature of it.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.729
And to be fair to Alvin Bragg,

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:57.830
when it comes to what he was saying

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.765
when he was running,

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.099
both of the candidates who were running

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.301
for the district attorney's

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.902
spot were asked about

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:03.870
how they would handle

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.405
a potential Trump investigation.

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:07.006
He cited his experience with it.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.708
You're on the House Oversight Committee.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.243
You're chairman of your committee.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:12.145
And along with other Republican chairmen,

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:13.212
have sent letters

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.348
to Alvin Bragg asking for his testimony,

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:15.915
something that

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.583
the counsel for the DA's office here in

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.152
Manhattan is pushing back on.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.186
Didn't President Trump

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.954
ask House Republicans

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.891
to investigate Alvin Bragg

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:26.993
No, I don't believe so.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:27.627
And I'm not going to speak

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:28.194
for the chairman,

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.028
but to my knowledge,

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.229
that has not occurred.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.531
You have members of Congress

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.532
who have actually watched

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:34.801
the weaponization of various agencies

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.302
of the federal government,

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.037
whether you want to talk about the FBI,

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.605
CDC, etc..

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:42.275
We already know that the FBI and CDC

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.776
have suppressed free

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.178
speech in the United States

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.779
and to social media companies.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.047
So our concern is

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:50.083
that you have elements of these agencies

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.151
who have been sending information

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.020
to Alvin Bragg's office,

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.054
because let's be very clear.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.456
You got elements of our agencies

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:57.623
who want to get rid of Trump

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.192
to obviously that something

00:05:59.192 --> 00:05:59.592
was going on

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.494
with the Mueller probe, etc..

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.496
So that's our concern.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.397
We want to make sure

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.498
that you don't have aspects

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:06.632
of the federal government

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.900
trying to aid in a bed

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.135
through the back door

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:10.937
the political persecution of

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:11.704
a former president

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:14.974
Okay.

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:15.241
I should

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.576
note, those are your allegations.

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:17.710
And we should note that

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.078
we have not actually seen the indictment

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.079
when those requests to him

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.481
and brag for his testimony

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:21.981
went through

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:22.648
Congressman Barr

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:23.549
and Donald to Florida,

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.252
thank you for joining us this morning.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:27.120
Thank you.

